From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: koyu <me@koyu.space>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 13:02:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/17] Merge the theme switch and wallpaper page into an
 appearance page

The Dark Theme switch moves from the "Before we get started" page, which
is removed, to the wallpaper page, now the appearance page. PrepareUtil
stays, it backs the switch. It
also gets an accent colour row with quick-appearance-kcm's palette, baked
into kdeglobals the same way and merged into the new user's along with
the theme. Picking BlossomUI's own blue clears the accent again.

The wallpaper can go on the desktop, the lock screen or both. Once the
user picks one, it replaces the glow behind setup. The glow crossfades
to a new accent colour over 5 seconds instead of blinking out.
